  theta13-cube pergrid production model; Track H = first Delta m^2-moving
  systematics arm).

  SCOPE: this file is consumed ONLY by sk_binned_engine.resolve_nuisance_spec
  (<path>.xml branch), which reads <nuisance name=".."><status>1</status>
  </nuisance> blocks in document order via a lightweight regex parser
  (_parse_xml_active). It activates the SAME 131 dials, in the SAME order, as
  claude-tmp/dm2/seeds_r2_fude_ccqe/r2_fude_ccqe.json:nuisance_names (byte-
  verified equal at generation time). Nominal values and sigmas for every dial
  live in the engine's CANONICAL_DIALS table, NOT in this file -- there is
  deliberately no <type>/<box>/<prior> content here. This is NOT a drop-in
  replacement for a full event-level PyNuFit Analysis XML: most of these 131
  dials (era-split detector systematics, momentum-banded flux ratios, the
  multi-GeV CCQE flavor norms, etc.) only exist inside the standalone binned
  engine and have no event-level PyNuFit tune-class counterpart.

  Equivalent invocations once this snapshot is vendored/resynced:
    nuisance_spec="R2FUDECCQE"                                   (named spec)
    nuisance_spec="path/to/SK2023_Atm_datafit_r2_fude_ccqe.xml"  (this file)
    nuisance_spec=json.load(open("r2_fude_ccqe.json"))["nuisance_names"]
  All three are verified identical, in order (see repo commit that added this
  file for the verification script).
-->
